      "message": "With `nextUpdateIndex()` now inside the try, `reloadOnce` may already have swapped `stack` and closed the old readers when it throws ESTALE, but `mergedReftable` is only rebuilt after the loop. If a later attempt then fails (deadline, or the FileNotFoundException rethrow), `mergedReftable` still points at the closed readers. `isUpToDate()` compares against the new `stack`, so it says up to date and reads hit ClosedChannelException until tables.list changes again. Building `mergedReftable` right after `reloadOnce` keeps the two in sync.\n\n\n```suggestion\n\t\t\t\treloadOnce(names, reopen);\n\t\t\t\tmergedReftable \u003d new MergedReftable(stack.stream()\n\t\t\t\t\t\t.map(x -\u003e x.reftableReader).collect(Collectors.toList()));\n\t\t\t\tcurr \u003d nextUpdateIndex();\n\t\t\t\tsuccess \u003d true;\n\t\t\t\tbreak;\n```",
